1
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:04,840
Since when did I become yours?

2
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:06,040
Well, that night we...

3
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:08,580
But is that something you should be telling other people?

4
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:11,140
And is it right

5
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:12,760
for him to wrap his arm around your neck and lean on your shoulder like that?

6
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:15,140
He's just my friend.

7
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:17,740
Anyone could tell from a mile away

8
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:19,300
that he's not just a friend.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,120
Well, that's his business.

10
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:24,960
It's none of your business.

11
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:25,880
Yeah.

12
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:27,240
It's none of my business,

13
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:28,820
but I don't like it.

14
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:31,220
Pond,

15
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:33,160
you're about to be an adult.

16
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:34,900
You have to work, you have to graduate.

17
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:36,700
Are you just going to focus on what I do or don't do,

18
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:38,900
and whether you like what I do? Is that it?

19
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:41,260
My goal...

20
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:43,360
is asking you to give me another chance.

21
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:47,540
Do you really have no other goals in life?

22
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:49,000
What about your goals for the future?

23
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,400
Don't you have anything else?

24
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:51,600
Well, my future...

25
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:53,540
has you in it.

26
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:10,300
Goal.

27
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:14,240
Okay.

28
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:17,080
Alright, everyone.

29
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:18,700
Listen up.

30
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:20,880
Today we're going to do an activity

31
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:22,860
where we split into groups,

32
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:26,460
to brainstorm new features for this resort

33
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:30,400
for our company's next 6-month plan.

34
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:31,920
How should we split into groups, ma'am?

35
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:34,720
Well, as you like, but...

36
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:37,100
the 2 groups must be equal in size.

37
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:41,400
Ma'am,

38
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:43,100
I have a question.

39
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:46,660
Are we just splitting into groups to brainstorm together,

40
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:48,920
or is it a competition between groups?

41
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:50,060
And is there a prize?

42
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:51,960
The winning team

43
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:53,200
gets nothing. There's no budget.

44
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,040
What?

45
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:56,440
Who would want to think? Where's the motivation in that?

46
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:57,540
Hello, everyone.

47
00:02:57,540 --> 00:02:58,980
I'm Tang-Oh.

48
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:00,620
I'm the owner of this resort.

49
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:03,920
Ah, I just overheard everyone talking about

50
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,980
creating a campaign for my resort.

51
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:07,680
So...

52
00:03:08,720 --> 00:03:09,660
how about this?

53
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:11,540
Whoever wins this campaign,

54
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:13,840
I'll give them a special gift voucher

55
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:14,580
for

56
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:17,120
a full year of free stays here.

57
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:17,760
How's that sound?

58
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:19,900
Wow, that's amazing!

59
00:03:21,940 --> 00:03:23,100
You're so generous!

60
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,060
Looks like everyone is ready.

61
00:03:28,060 --> 00:03:30,820
So let's split into groups. Go ahead!

62
00:03:30,820 --> 00:03:32,620
Split up and choose who you want to be with.

63
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,040
Uh, wait a second.

64
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:42,620
Make them equal.

65
00:03:42,620 --> 00:03:44,660
Two groups of 3 people, right?

66
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:46,200
Right now, there are too many on one side.

67
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:49,640
Hmm.

68
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:51,340
Can someone switch over?

69
00:03:51,340 --> 00:03:53,080
You can come over to this side too.

70
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:55,000
Then I'll go over here.

71
00:03:57,480 --> 00:03:59,360
Okay.

72
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:01,840
Discuss among yourselves, go ahead.

73
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:08,400
P'Best,

74
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,260
hold on,

75
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:12,000
I'll go get a cold drink for you.

76
00:04:14,780 --> 00:04:15,960
I'm not giving it to you, though.

77
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:22,200
P'Best,

78
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:25,140
who is that guy?

79
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:27,320
Oh,

80
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:28,400
P'Tang-Oh.

81
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:30,660
He's been P'Dan's friend since high school.

82
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:32,140
But in university,

83
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:33,960
Dan went to study in Chiang Mai,

84
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:35,200
while Tang-Oh went to Bangkok.

85
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:38,120
In the meantime, though, they kept in touch the whole time.

86
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:41,060
Is that something I really need to know?

87
00:04:41,060 --> 00:04:41,760
Well,

88
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:44,200
if you don't want to know, I'll stop telling you.

89
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:47,960
I heard that P'Ton

90
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:49,200
wants a graphics card.

91
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:51,600
He got a fun game, you know.

92
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:53,440
No wonder.

93
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:55,120
Lately he's been quiet and hardly replies.

94
00:04:55,940 --> 00:04:56,760
Yeah.

95
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:58,620
Did P'Ton tell you the specs?

96
00:04:58,620 --> 00:05:00,700
Yeah, so you tell me about this heir guy first,

97
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:02,460
and how he's related to P'Dan.

98
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:05,240
You tell me, I tell you.

99
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:06,940
Well, deal?

100
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:20,060
Hello?

101
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:21,400
Yeah, what's up?

102
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:25,000
Hey bro, I heard you went on a company outing out of town.

103
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,600
How do you know I'm here?

104
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:27,760
Come on, I'm Jemin, bro.

105
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:29,860
Who's Jemin?

106
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:33,800
Jemin, your die-hard fan! I know everything about you.

107
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:35,760
So are you going to be there the whole time?

108
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:36,880
Uh...

109
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:38,720
Do you have time to come see me?

110
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:41,180
Do you have time to come see me, then?

111
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:43,640
Why do you sound like that? Is something wrong?

112
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:44,480
Yeah.

113
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:46,700
Hey, go on, tell me.

114
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:48,240
P'Dan...

115
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:49,760
he had an ex before me.

116
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:51,160
Holy shit.

117
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:53,440
So you weren't P'Dan's first, bro?

118
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:01,080
Damn, I really didn't think you'd actually come.

119
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:02,680
My university is just right here.

120
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:03,220
See,

121
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:05,880
I usually come here to drink coffee and work quite often.

122
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:09,100
I never thought this place was your competitor's resort.

123
00:06:09,620 --> 00:06:11,740
Are you here to encourage me or to tear me down?

124
00:06:11,740 --> 00:06:13,500
I'm here to encourage you, bro.

125
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:14,780
But just now,

126
00:06:14,780 --> 00:06:16,780
I saw P'Dan walking with some random guy.

127
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:19,880
The one who's less handsome than me?

128
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:22,620
Woah, handsomeness is just a matter of taste, bro.

129
00:06:22,620 --> 00:06:24,920
It depends on what kind of type he likes, right?

130
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,280
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

131
00:06:26,280 --> 00:06:26,900
Huh?

132
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:29,540
Yeah, I know. Why are you getting so annoyed?

133
00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:32,300
You're always number one to me, man.

134
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:34,060
I'm not annoyed at you, alright?

135
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:37,920
Because I saw P'Dan walking with him.

136
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:42,140
That's not it, man.

137
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:44,840
He called P'Dan 'darling'.

138
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:47,500
And P'Dan still walked away with him.

139
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:49,020
And what about me?

140
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:52,200
I think, like...

141
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:53,480
P'Dan...

142
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:54,880
shouldn't be that hard.

143
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:57,180
What do you mean by that?

144
00:06:57,180 --> 00:06:59,720
Well, you already got P'Dan that night.

145
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:01,160
Others might...

146
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:04,080
Watch your mouth.

147
00:07:04,080 --> 00:07:05,720
Or my foot's going to hit your mouth one day.

148
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:07,240
Feisty, feisty!

149
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:10,020
Why do you like him so much, man?

150
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:11,520
At first, I thought that...

151
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:15,000
you just wanted to get back at him for suddenly disappearing.

152
00:07:15,180 --> 00:07:17,140
You just wanted to win over him, right?

153
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:19,040
I want him back with me.

154
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:21,120
But not...

155
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:22,900
getting back at him the way you think.

156
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:27,520
I think, bro...

157
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:28,260
this guy...

158
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:30,160
you can just play around with him, no need to be serious.

159
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:31,720
If you're going to be serious for once,

160
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:33,160
why does it have to be this guy?

161
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:34,640
And what's wrong with this guy?

162
00:07:37,460 --> 00:07:38,940
I'm asking for real, bro.

163
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:40,800
Is he really that attractive?

164
00:07:41,220 --> 00:07:43,900
Everyone in the faculty says he's not right for you,

165
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:45,920
and yet you're still chasing after him.

166
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:51,140
Hey, and look at how P'Dan treats you.

167
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:53,860
He's nothing like how he was in high school.

168
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:56,060
Being with P'Kaen suits you way better.

169
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:19,640
You saw that, right? That I was about to rush to Pond? / Yeah.

170
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:22,240
But Pond jumped straight to Dan.

171
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:22,900
Yeah.

172
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:23,720
I was stunned.

173
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:25,860
Thinking about it, I still feel...

174
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:26,900
that Pond and Dan...

175
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:29,300
are totally wrong for each other, girl.

176
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:31,200
Girl, the Pond-Dan pair is just...

177
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:33,340
such a bad match. / Right?

178
00:08:33,340 --> 00:08:34,380
Pardon?

179
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:37,440
Girls, what are you talking about?

180
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:41,360
We're talking about the activity to submit today, boss.

181
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,580
Very good.

182
00:08:42,580 --> 00:08:44,280
Don't forget to submit it this afternoon.

183
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:44,920
We won't forget.

184
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:45,920
Alright!

185
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:47,320
No skipping, okay?

186
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:49,140
We won't skip.

187
00:08:49,140 --> 00:08:49,860
Dan,

188
00:08:52,560 --> 00:08:54,340
don't forget to submit yours too.

189
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:56,040
Don't skip, okay?

190
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:57,820
Here's some water.

191
00:08:57,820 --> 00:08:58,920
Thanks.

192
00:08:58,920 --> 00:09:00,240
Thanks, Dan.

193
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:04,040
Do you think he heard us?

194
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:04,620
Yes.

195
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:10,280
Well, I'll...

196
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:11,680
go to the bathroom first.

197
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:12,760
Bathroom.

198
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:15,600
Okay, then let me keep talking to them,

199
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:17,080
and we'll head back later.

200
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:19,880
Did he hear us?

201
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:21,580
I feel guilty.

202
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:23,140
I think...

203
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:25,020
Dan heard us.

204
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:26,520
I know, right?

205
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,620
You started it first.

206
00:09:30,620 --> 00:09:32,480
You were the one talking to me!

207
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:01,760
Oh, Ton.

208
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:02,320
Oh.

209
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:04,640
I thought you were P'Dan.

210
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:06,280
Did you come looking for P'Dan?

211
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,440
Uh...

212
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:12,360
Actually, I...

213
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:14,880
came specifically to find you.

214
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,960
I just found out you're from around here.

215
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,160
Could you take me around for a tour?

216
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:24,380
Hmm.

217
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:25,520
You want to go sightseeing?

218
00:10:25,860 --> 00:10:26,620
Sure.

219
00:10:26,860 --> 00:10:28,920
Over there, there's a nice place.

220
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:30,500
Do you want to go?

221
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:31,500
I'd love to.

222
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:32,220
Okay.

223
00:10:32,540 --> 00:10:33,320
Let's go.

224
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,620
We should go out together like this

225
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:01,620
more often like before, P'Dan.

226
00:11:01,620 --> 00:11:02,900
When did you get here?

227
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:08,400
I came when you were sitting there daydreaming about the resort owner, I guess.

228
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:11,380
Whatever you say.

229
00:11:11,380 --> 00:11:13,040
I can't stop you anyway.

230
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:16,060
P'Best told me

231
00:11:16,060 --> 00:11:17,940
that you two have known each other since high school.

232
00:11:19,260 --> 00:11:20,800
But I feel like...

233
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:22,200
he still...

234
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:23,380
He's...

235
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:25,220
a good friend to me.

236
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:28,100
What about me, then?

237
00:11:28,860 --> 00:11:30,080
Am I not good to you at all?

238
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:36,340
If you're going to talk about that night, I think it might have been...

239
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:39,380
just a mistake.

240
00:11:40,780 --> 00:11:41,620
A mistake?

241
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:44,760
If we take that night out of the picture,

242
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:47,780
when you're with me,

243
00:11:47,780 --> 00:11:49,440
don't you feel anything at all?

244
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:56,300
Well, I think...

245
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:00,820
I might not be suitable for you.

246
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:03,320
P'Dan,

247
00:12:05,060 --> 00:12:06,560
I really like you, you know?

248
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:08,220
When you're serious with me...

249
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:11,960
nobody has ever been this serious about me before.

250
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:14,980
Compared to that P'Tang-Oh guy,

251
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:16,980
I'd definitely lose.

252
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:19,080
But could you be a referee...

253
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:21,860
who is just a little bit biased toward me?

254
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,900
Please give me another chance.

255
